# .agent-vm.shadow — copy to <project-root>/.agent-vm.shadow
#
# Paths (relative to the project root) to back with persistent VM-local storage.
#
# Each listed directory is bind-mounted over with a dedicated directory on the
# VM's own disk, so the host copy is shadowed (never read or written) and the VM
# gets its own independent contents. This is useful for arch-specific build
# artifacts like node_modules: `npm i` on the macOS host installs the darwin
# build while `npm i` inside the Linux VM installs the linux build, and because
# the project dir is shared they would otherwise overwrite each other.
#
# Notes:
#   - Backing storage persists across VM stop/start, so `npm install` runs once
#     and is reused. It is removed automatically when the VM is destroyed.
#   - Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   - Paths must be relative to the project root (no leading '/' or '..').

frontend/node_modules
